===Land tenure===

Agricultural land in Balisca is held under three primary tenure systems:

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Tenure Type !! Description !! % of Agricultural Land
|-
| '''Agricultural cooperatives''' || Land owned collectively by farmer-members; democratic governance || 62%
|-
| '''Communal tenure''' || Land owned by communes; allocated to members based on need || 28%
|-
| '''Family farms''' || Small individually-operated farms within land trust framework || 10%
|}

The [[Communal Land Trust Act]] (1921) prohibits the sale of agricultural land for speculative purposes. Land may only be transferred to other farmers, cooperatives, or communes, or returned to the land trust for reallocation. This system has prevented land concentration and maintained access for new farmers.

