===Wine industry===

{{Main|Wine industry in Balisca}}

Balisca is a significant wine producer, with the industry centered in the [[Piedmont]] Central Valley. The confederation's wine industry is distinctive for its cooperative structure—most vineyards and wineries are owned and operated by farmer cooperatives—and its emphasis on organic and biodynamic production methods.

Key wine regions include the [[Nova Barcelona]] Valley, noted for premium red wines including Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, and Carménère; the [[Syracuse]] Hills, known for white wines including Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, and Riesling; the [[Cerdanya]] Plains, which specialize in sparkling wines using traditional method production; and the [[Aprica]] Coast, producing cool-climate wines including Pinot Noir and Chardonnay.

Wine exports totalled ε9.2 billion in 2023, making it agriculture's largest export category by value.

