Sheep farming is particularly important in the southern grasslands and highland regions, while pig and poultry production is concentrated near urban centers. Alpaca and llama raising is traditional in the [[Matarrañya]] highlands and provides valuable fiber for textile production.

==Forestry==

{{Main|Forestry in Balisca}}

===Forest resources===

Balisca possesses extensive forest resources, covering approximately 1,124,000 km² (39.5% of total land area). The majority of this forest is temperate rainforest in the [[Marañón basin]], the largest temperate rainforest in the world. Additional forest types include montane forests in the highlands, subtropical forests in the north, and subpolar forests in the far south.

Forest ownership follows the same cooperative and communal patterns as agricultural land:

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Ownership Type !! % of Forest Land
|-
| '''Community forest cooperatives''' || 48%
|-
| '''Communal forests''' || 35%
|-
| '''Confederal protected forests''' || 15%
|-
| '''Private (small holdings)''' || 2%
|}

===Sustainable forestry===

The [[Sustainable Forestry Act]] (1988) established strict standards for forest management. All commercial forestry must be conducted under sustainable management plans that ensure forest regeneration, protect biodiversity, and respect the rights of forest-dependent communities. Clear-cutting is prohibited, and selective harvesting is the standard practice.

Key forestry products include sawn timber (72.4 million m³ annually), pulp and paper (32.8 million tons annually), engineered wood (18.2 million m³ annually), and non-timber products valued at ε3.6 billion annually, including mushrooms, medicinal plants, and berries.

The forestry sector has been at the forefront of Balisca's [[W:Mass timber|mass timber]] construction industry, with engineered wood products increasingly replacing steel and concrete in construction.

===Reforestation and conservation===

Since the [[Baliscan Revolution]], reforestation programs have restored approximately 45,000 km² of degraded forest land. The [[Ecological Action]] program (1995) established a goal of maintaining forest cover above 35% of total land area, a target that has been exceeded. Protected forest areas cover 168,000 km², representing 15% of total forest land.

==Fishing and aquaculture==

{{Main|Fishing industry in Balisca}}

===Marine fisheries===

Balisca's extensive coastline along the [[Salsipuedes Sea]] and the [[Aethiopian Ocean]] supports a significant fishing industry. The confederation's [[W:Exclusive economic zone|exclusive economic zone]] covers approximately 1.2 million km², encompassing some of the most productive fishing grounds in Abyala.

The fishing industry is organized through [[Fishing cooperative|fishing cooperatives]] that own vessels, processing facilities, and marketing operations. This structure ensures that fishing communities benefit directly from the resource and provides incentives for sustainable management.

